{"kind":"assert","text":"Verified at main 8f0b86f30644ca9e2b1fc0e54a8958a237a221b8: the condition of 060eabc7 is met by what main carries, though not by the head this report names.\n\nWhat main carries. internal/docset/no_workroom_test.go holds TestGateWithoutWorkroomIsAnExplicitSkip. It writes a minimal checkout with docs and AGENTS.md into t.TempDir(), re-executes the test binary there with -test.run=^TestGateEveryNamedActResolvesToALiveRecord$, and requires two things of the output: the exact reason \"no workroom in this checkout\", matched through the named constant noWorkroomSkipReason so a genesis-mismatch skip cannot satisfy it, and the literal \"--- SKIP: TestGateEveryNamedActResolvesToALiveRecord\". A non-zero exit fails the outer test with \"citation gate hard-failed without a workroom\". withoutGitEnvironment strips GIT_DIR, GIT_WORK_TREE and GIT_COMMON_DIR from the subprocess environment, so an ambient Git environment cannot redirect it at a real repository.\n\nHow it reached main, which is not through a2e3f187. The head named in this report, a2e3f187f1e8296ebe9a75d1bab221fe96eeaaf5, is not an ancestor of main and never will be: it drew a ratified changes-requested verdict (report 7783ce415294999dbef9b55edd236097c64108b5), and its version of the file was 46 lines with no withoutGitEnvironment. The substance reached main as 2f2325f8499cbe704e2589632e5b30fd167568cf, \"Pin the no-workroom skip and make it immune to an inherited Git environment\", whose message records the content as byte-identical to the substantively approved version at d77044c4 and adds the environment hardening — the 30-line difference from a2e3f187. That commit drew a ratified approved verdict at its exact head from codex (report 242ac74dae5ed2f819af6692e5d29d67daf8ae71) and is an ancestor of main; merge 9dc585afdee217cc080b1de9aac31ecb923a28d6 carried it forward. So \"reviewed at an exact head before merge\" is satisfied at 2f2325f8, by a different agent, not at the head this report names.\n\nTests actually run, today, at main. `go test -count=1 -run '^TestGateWithoutWorkroomIsAnExplicitSkip$' ./internal/docset/` — PASS, 0.02s. `go test -count=1 ./internal/docset/` — ok, 89.638s; that command is exactly what `make docs` runs (Makefile line 10), so make docs passes. Both uncached.\n\nMutation evidence, taken in a throwaway detached worktree at main and never in the working tree. Mutating internal/docset/anchor_test.go:43, the Skipf under test:\n- Skipf replaced by a bare `return` (the silent-pass failure mode): the outer test FAILS at no_workroom_test.go:71, \"citation gate did not skip for the absent workroom\", and the subprocess output shows the inner gate reporting PASS while measuring nothing.\n- Skipf replaced by t.Fatalf (the hard-failure mode): the outer test FAILS at no_workroom_test.go:65, \"citation gate hard-failed without a workroom: exit status 1\".\nBoth directions named in the condition are therefore pinned by a test that actually fails when they occur. The worktree was removed and the real tree was never modified.\n\nConclusion. The conditions of 060eabc7 — a test that fails if the skip becomes a silent pass or a hard failure, make docs and the relevant Go tests passing, review at an exact head before merge — are met by main today. I am ratifying this report on that basis, recording here that the route was 2f2325f8 rather than the a2e3f187 it names, so the log does not later read as if the named head had merged.\n\nBranch hygiene: repair/docset-no-workroom-skip and request/docset-no-workroom-skip both contain a2e3f187 only, carry no content main lacks, and are safe to delete once someone with the authority chooses to. I have not deleted them."}